    {
      "external_id": "C12-BIO-CH22-22.3.2-STEPS-TO-CREATE-A-PIE-CHART-WITH-EXAMPLE",
      "chapter": "pk-punjab/xii/biology/c12-bio/ch22",
      "topic": "pk-punjab/xii/biology/c12-bio/ch22/u-steps-to-create-a-pie-chart-with-example",
      "title": "Steps to create a pie chart with example",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "779562c7-0658-5de6-b1a6-2ee025d3b016",
          "pdf_from": 199,
          "pdf_to": 200,
          "note": "Steps to create a pie chart with example: a main subheading of 22.3.2 Pie Chart, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 199-200."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A biology class surveys 100 students to find their blood types. The results are as follows:"
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Table: Surevy results of student blood types",
            "header": [
              "Blood type",
              "Number of students (frequency)"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "A",
                "30"
              ],
              [
                "B",
                "20"
              ],
              [
                "AB",
                "10"
              ],
              [
                "O",
                "40"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 1: Organize data",
            "bold": [
              "Step 1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Arrange the categorical data in a table, noting the frequency or total for each category as shown in table….."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 2: Add up all frequency values to get the total sum",
            "bold": [
              "Step 2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Total number of students= 30+20+10+40 = 100"
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Sum of frequency and sector angle of each blood type",
            "header": [
              "Sum of frequency",
              "Blood Type",
              "No. of Student",
              "Sector angle = Sum of values"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "30",
                "A",
                "30",
                "30/100 × 360° = 108°"
              ],
              [
                "20+30=50",
                "B",
                "20",
                "20/100 × 360° = 72°"
              ],
              [
                "10+50=60",
                "AB",
                "10",
                "10/100 × 360° = 36°"
              ],
              [
                "40+60=100",
                "O",
                "40",
                "40/100 × 360° = 144°"
              ],
              [
                "",
                "Total",
                "n =100",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 3: Calculate the sector angles (Sector angle = Category value/ total value X 100)",
            "book_errors": [
              "X 100"
            ],
            "bold": [
              "Step 3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A= 30/100 X 360° = 108° %",
            "book_errors": [
              "108° %"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "B= 20/100 X 360° = 72° %",
            "book_errors": [
              "72° %"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "AB= 10/100 X 360° = 36° %",
            "book_errors": [
              "36° %"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "O= 40/100 X 360° = 144° %",
            "book_errors": [
              "144° %"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "text": "Sector angle = (category value / total value) × 360°, not × 100. The angles are degrees, not per cent: A = 108°, B = 72°, AB = 36° and O = 144°, which add up to 360°.",
            "title": "Book correction"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 4: Draw the pie chart",
            "bold": [
              "Step 4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Draw a circle by using a protractor, draw each sector angle in sequence (clock wise or counter clockwise) using the calculated angles in step 3. Start with a reference line (radius). Use different colours/shades to differentiate each category."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Step 5: Label and title",
            "bold": [
              "Step 5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Clearly label each sector and provide a legend if needed. Add a descriptive title to the chart."
          },
          {
            "type": "diagram",
            "$asset": "c12-bio-ch22-fig-pie-chart",
            "alt": "Pie chart titled Distribution of blood types among students. Starting at the top and going clockwise: A blue, 30%, 30; B orange, 20%, 20; AB grey, 10%, 10; O yellow, 40%, 40. A legend below names A, B, AB and O.",
            "caption": "Pie chart showing distribution of blood types among students (original drawing after the textbook's unnumbered figure)."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
